From a1c98c1c613c388f4157947953a9081b63d8a52d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristian Rickert <kristian@apache.org>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:19:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] openvino: store weights in the plugin cache on CPU and
 GPU

With GGML_OPENVINO_CACHE_DIR the backend requests
CacheMode::OPTIMIZE_SIZE on CPU and GPU, OpenVINO's weightless cache: a
blob stores the compiled kernels and the weights are read from the model
again when the blob is loaded.

On an Arc B70 (OpenVINO 2026.4.1), with whisper.cpp graphs and two
models in one process, a process that starts from such a cache does not
behave like the one that filled it. The first state of each model
decodes one second of silence differently (190080 decoder compute nodes
in place of 1296: the result fails whisper's quality check and runs
through every fallback temperature), while the second state, on the
same compiled models, decodes as before. And compile_model for the conv
graph of the second model can die with SIGSEGV in memcpy under
libigdrcl.so, called from the GPU plugin, reading a host buffer:
seven boots of seven with one order of the two models, none with the
other order. No boot that fills the cache does either.

Without a cache directory, and with OPTIMIZE_SPEED, every boot decodes
the same and none crashes, and the boot from the cache is faster
(0.35 s of warmup for the first state, 1.6 s when compiling, 8.5 s from
the weightless cache). The blobs then hold their weights, as the ones
of GGML_OPENVINO_COMPILED_MODEL_CACHE_DIR already do.

NPU keeps its own cache settings.
---
 ggml/src/ggml-openvino/ggml-openvino-extra.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-openvino/ggml-openvino-extra.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-openvino/ggml-openvino-extra.cpp
index e485c45..62c9d0f 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-openvino/ggml-openvino-extra.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-openvino/ggml-openvino-extra.cpp
@@ -183,7 +183,9 @@ void ggml_openvino_device_config::init() {
         }
     } else if (cache_dir && strlen(cache_dir) > 0) {
         compile_config.insert(ov::cache_dir(cache_dir));
-        compile_config.insert(ov::cache_mode(ov::CacheMode::OPTIMIZE_SIZE));
+        // Not OPTIMIZE_SIZE: a GPU blob without its weights did not reproduce the model that wrote it
+        // (whisper graphs on Arc B70: different logits on first use, SIGSEGV in compile_model).
+        compile_config.insert(ov::cache_mode(ov::CacheMode::OPTIMIZE_SPEED));
     }
 
     if (ggml_openvino_getenv_int("GGML_OPENVINO_PROFILING") >= 2) {
